     The sshhmmccttll() function returns the value 0 if successful; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The sshhmmccttll() system call will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           Invalid operation, or no shared memory segment was
                        found corresponding to _s_h_m_i_d.

     [EPERM]            The calling process's effective uid does not match the
                        uid of the shared memory segment's owner or creator.

     [EACCES]           Permission denied due to mismatch between operation
                        and mode of shared memory segment.

